8443\nab1ef694-0826-4671-a22c-565fc2d282ec    Service_openshif    tcp        172.30.196.123:443      10.128.0.33:8443,10.129.0.64:8443,10.130.0.37:8443\nb1fb34d3-0944-4770-9ee3-2683e7a630e2    Service_openshif    tcp        172.30.158.93:8443      10.129.0.13:8443\n95811c11-56e2-4877-be1e-c78ccb3a82a9    Service_openshif    tcp        172.30.46.85:9001       10.130.0.16:9001\n4baba1d1-b873-4535-884c-3f6fc07a50fd    Service_openshif    tcp        172.30.28.87:443        10.129.0.26:8443\n6c2e1c90-f0ca-484e-8a8e-40e71442110a    Service_openshif    udp        172.30.0.10:53          10.128.0.13:5353,10.128.2.6:5353,10.129.0.39:5353,10.129.2.6:5353,10.130.0.11:5353,10.131.0.9:5353\n"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>From this truncated output you can see there are many OVN-Kubernetes load balancers. Load balancers in OVN-Kubernetes are representations of services.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      </li>
      </ol>
      </li>
      <li>
      Display the options available with the <code>ovn-nbctl</code> command by entering the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc exec -n openshift-ovn-kubernetes -it ovnkube-node-55xs2 \\\n-c nbdb ovn-nbctl --help"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
